{"id": "EUVD-2026-103816", "enisaUuid": "b3b4e054-0e95-35b9-9f26-6ea809a76cd2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel_pcie: fix plen overflow in btintel_pcie_recv_frame()\n\nplen is u16 and computed as HDR_SIZE + dlen. For ACL/ISO frames dlen\nis a 16-bit field, so a value >= 0xFFFC wraps the sum, bypassing the\n\"skb->len < plen\" check and letting skb_trim() truncate the packet.\n\nWiden plen to u32 so the addition cannot wrap.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:24:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3a3842c109ac130c6db3aa0014cc8cd344928ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3b5e6da4ba6485bffda9753d8339c28855207aa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2cb5ea1dc8cf829816370fc1399e6a1d2d1bca9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7dbeb6935ac331b0cba6c41cabd8e9d02d5f64ea"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98731", "GHSA-8674-5775-h37c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ed26e08-9bac-3511-96cb-ee58759ed846", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "4b06a931-5374-315f-8ba4-683f3ef82d01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <7dbeb6935ac331b0cba6c41cabd8e9d02d5f64ea"}, {"id": "844d07a6-e401-3697-9027-e0db03181ef2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "8bd186ce-ad51-39a3-a486-ccc55cc132ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9badeb8d-313a-3bce-bbe0-5771c6b1ccf8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a203b3d7-c52a-3782-86d0-920fa337e76a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2b636b3f788d10486a6691ad6dd3ec4c93bd78e <c3b5e6da4ba6485bffda9753d83